<!-- ══ ROADMAP ════════════════════════════════════ -->
<section class="section section-alt">
    <div class="container-r">
        <div class="tag">Your Journey</div>
        <h2 style="text-align:center;margin-bottom:40px;">CA Course Roadmap: From Class 12 to Chartered Accountant</h2>
        <div class="roadmap">

            <div class="road-step">
                <div class="road-left"><div class="road-dot">1</div><div class="road-line"></div></div>
                <div class="road-body">
                    <h3>Class 12 Pass</h3>
                    <p>After completing your Class 12 board exams from any stream (Commerce, Science, or Arts), you become eligible to register for the CA Foundation course with ICAI. You can register during your Class 12 itself to save time.</p>
                </div>
            </div>

            <div class="road-step">
                <div class="road-left"><div class="road-dot">2</div><div class="road-line"></div></div>
                <div class="road-body">
                    <h3>CA Foundation (4 months preparation)</h3>
                    <p>The entry-level exam covering Principles of Accounting, Business Laws, Business Mathematics, and Economics. Exams are held in May and November. A well-prepared student clears Foundation in the first or second attempt.</p>
                </div>
            </div>

            <div class="road-step">
                <div class="road-left"><div class="road-dot">3</div><div class="road-line"></div></div>
                <div class="road-body">
                    <h3>CA Intermediate (8–12 months preparation)</h3>
                    <p>Eight subjects across two groups. Students begin their 3-year Articleship (practical training) after clearing at least one group of CA Intermediate. The Intermediate exam can be attempted group-by-group or both groups together.</p>
                </div>
            </div>

            <div class="road-step">
                <div class="road-left"><div class="road-dot">4</div><div class="road-line"></div></div>
                <div class="road-body">
                    <h3>Articleship (3 Years)</h3>
                    <p>Mandatory practical training under a practising CA. During Articleship, students gain real-world exposure to auditing, taxation, and financial advisory work. CA Final preparation typically happens simultaneously during the later years of Articleship.</p>
                </div>
            </div>

            <div class="road-step">
                <div class="road-left"><div class="road-dot">5</div><div class="road-line"></div></div>
                <div class="road-body">
                    <h3>CA Final (12–18 months preparation)</h3>
                    <p>The most advanced level, covering eight highly specialised subjects. Candidates appear for CA Final in the last six months of Articleship or after completing it. Clearing CA Final earns you the prestigious ICAI membership.</p>
                </div>
            </div>

            <div class="road-step">
                <div class="road-left"><div class="road-dot" style="background:var(--gold);color:var(--maroon);">✓</div></div>
                <div class="road-body">
                    <h3>Become a Chartered Accountant</h3>
                    <p>After clearing CA Final, you apply for ICAI membership and are officially designated a Chartered Accountant. You are now qualified to practice independently or join any organisation as a CA professional. The journey typically takes 4.5–5 years from Class 12.</p>
                </div>
            </div>

        </div>
    </div>
</section>

