            <div class="faq-body"><p>The CA qualification offers high earning potential (starting at ₹6–12 LPA and growing significantly with experience), global recognition, job security, and the freedom to practice independently. Every business needs a CA for auditing, taxation, and compliance — making it one of the most evergreen and future-proof careers in India. Raipur and Chhattisgarh have seen significant growth in demand for qualified CAs as the region industrialises rapidly.</p></div>
        </details>

        <details>
            <summary>What are the eligibility criteria for CA Foundation?</summary>
            <div class="faq-body"><p>To be eligible for CA Foundation, you must have passed Class 12 (10+2) from a recognised board in any stream. There is no minimum percentage requirement from ICAI for registration, though most competitive students have 50% or above. You can register with ICAI for CA Foundation while in Class 12 and appear for the Foundation exam after clearing your board exams.</p></div>
